        "source":  "Microsoft AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://news.microsoft.com/signal/articles/how-to-build-an-ai-agent-guide/",
        "date":  "2026-08-10",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Microsoft outlines a five-step framework for building AI agents using Microsoft 365 Copilot without requiring coding experience, emphasizing that agents differ from chatbots by taking autonomous action. The guide walks users through defining a problem, selecting a starting point, configuring agent behavior, connecting knowledge sources, and iterating through testing. The piece positions agent-building as an accessible skill for any knowledge worker.",
        "execSummary":  "Microsoft is deliberately lowering the barrier to agent creation by framing it as a no-code, five-step process accessible to non-technical employees — a strategic move to accelerate enterprise agent deployment through the existing Microsoft 365 user base. For enterprise leaders, this signals that agent proliferation will come from business units, not just IT, raising new questions around governance, data access controls, and quality assurance. The \u0027connect knowledge sources\u0027 step is particularly significant: agents tied to live enterprise data become decision-support tools, not just task automators. Leaders should establish an agent governance policy before self-service agent creation outpaces oversight capacity.",
        "vendorLean":  "Microsoft — positions Microsoft 365 Copilot as the primary agent-building platform",
