        "source":  "Google AI Blog",
        "url":  "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/productivity-features-gemini-live/",
        "date":  "2026-08-26",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Google rolled out a major productivity upgrade to Gemini Live, enabling voice-controlled delegation of complex, multi-step tasks across Google apps hands-free. New capabilities include Spark integration for automated task management, Daily Brief for morning summaries, hands-free email management, and Personal Intelligence that remembers past conversations for personalized assistance. The update positions Gemini Live as an always-on voice agent layer across the Google ecosystem.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s Gemini Live upgrade crosses a threshold from voice assistant to voice agent: users can now delegate multi-step workflows across Google apps using natural speech, with the system retaining context across sessions via Personal Intelligence. For enterprise leaders in customer support and operations, this previews what always-on AI assistance looks like for frontline workers who cannot pause to type — a paradigm shift for field service, logistics, and contact center roles. The Daily Brief and email management features also signal that AI is moving from reactive tool to proactive chief-of-staff, managing attention rather than just answering questions. Watch for enterprise governance questions around persistent memory: what data is retained, who owns it, and how it is secured.",
        "vendorLean":  "Google — promotes Gemini app and Google Workspace ecosystem as the voice-agent platform",
