        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Gartner research surveying over 1,300 organizational leaders found that fewer than a quarter of enterprises have successfully scaled AI across multiple business units. Despite this, 85% of tech leaders plan to increase AI investments in the coming year, with organizations lacking clear ROI measurement and disciplined project assessment frameworks struggling most.",
        "execSummary":  "Gartner\u0027s survey of 1,300+ enterprise leaders exposes a stark gap: three out of four organizations are failing to scale AI past isolated pilots even as 85% plan to increase AI spending — a recipe for escalating waste. For senior leaders, this is a governance and prioritization problem: the organizations scaling successfully share disciplined ROI measurement frameworks and clear business-unit ownership. The key implication is that more budget alone will not close the scaling gap — what\u0027s needed is the organizational infrastructure (data readiness, change management, ROI accountability) to carry pilots to production. Leaders should audit scaling readiness before approving 2027 AI budget increases.",
