        "summary":  "The article examines how organizations can move agentic AI from isolated pilots to enterprise-wide deployment. NiCE\u0027s chief operating officer explains that successful scaling requires connecting AI initiatives to clear business objectives, redesigning workflows rather than layering AI onto existing processes, and treating agents as integrated systems with full data and backend access.",
        "execSummary":  "NiCE\u0027s operating model for scaling agentic AI offers a practical playbook: tie each agent to a measurable business outcome, redesign the workflow the agent operates in rather than patching AI onto legacy processes, and ensure agents have the data and backend connectivity they need to act. For customer support and operations leaders, this reframes the agent deployment question from \u0027which tool do we buy\u0027 to \u0027which workflow do we redesign first.\u0027 The critical watch-out is that agents layered on broken or fragmented processes will amplify dysfunction, not eliminate it. This piece is sponsored content but the operational guidance is grounded and transferable.",
