        "date":  "2026-09-02",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Jabil, a global manufacturer with 100+ sites across 30+ countries, adopted a simplify-first approach — integrating fragmented systems and establishing a unified data backbone using SAP solutions before layering in AI and automation. This strategic sequencing enables faster response to supply chain disruptions and improved operational resilience across regions.",
        "execSummary":  "Jabil\u0027s global AI transformation story offers a clear lesson: data and systems integration must precede AI deployment at scale, and organizations that try to skip this foundation step will find AI amplifying fragmentation rather than solving it. For enterprise technology leaders, the \u0027simplify first, innovate second\u0027 discipline is the most transferable insight — particularly for large, multi-site organizations where data silos are the primary AI scaling barrier. The implication for support and operations leaders is that AI capability investments made before achieving a unified data foundation will likely underdeliver. This is sponsored content tied to SAP but the architectural principle holds broadly.",
